    {
      "key": "lesson:pl-no-articles",
      "content": {
        "type": "lesson",
        "id": "pl-no-articles",
        "languageId": "pl"
      },
      "published": {
        "video": {
          "purpose": "lesson-explanation",
          "url": "pl/lesson/pl-no-articles/video-ee1694087cdb.mp4",
          "posterUrl": "pl/lesson/pl-no-articles/poster-ee1694087cdb.jpg",
          "captionsUrl": "pl/lesson/pl-no-articles/captions-ee1694087cdb.vtt",
          "captionsLanguage": "en",
          "durationSeconds": 96.01,
          "width": 1280,
          "height": 720,
          "narrator": "Marek",
          "transcript": [
            {
              "text": "Polish has no articles. Why there is no word for a, an or the, and what to do about it.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "Polish has no articles: there are no separate words for a, an or the.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "A bare noun can therefore mean a cat or the cat, and the meaning comes from the situation.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "When you translate into English, choose a, an or the from the context.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "Mam kota.",
              "language": "pl",
              "translation": "I have a cat."
            },
            {
              "text": "There is no word for a. The ending of kota changes because it is the object of the verb; that is a later topic.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "Kot śpi.",
              "language": "pl",
              "translation": "The cat is sleeping."
            },
            {
              "text": "It could also mean A cat is sleeping, depending on the situation.",
              "language": "en"
            },
            {
              "text": "Mam psa.",
              "language": "pl",
              "translation": "I have a dog."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read the examples below the video at your own pace.",
              "language": "en"
            }
          ]
        },
        "audio": []
      },
      "sourceHash": "78d283e193f4dea74c1cf7c7c0f16c05a7f9a932a5a94caeaf2a8aefd89b3d7a",
      "narratorId": "marek",
